 "short_name": "Ndlambe",
 "_doc": "Emunsoft 'TAX INVOICE/STATEMENT OF ACCOUNT': header (Account Number, Account Date, Street, Deposit), a METER READINGS table (meter, type, old/new reading, reading date, reading type, consumption) and an ACCOUNT DETAILS ledger (DATE CODE DESCRIPTION UNITS TARIFF VALUE, ex-VAT values, one VAT line for the whole bill), aging and a remittance TOTAL DUE. Fingerprint: Ndlambe's own VAT number + 'NDLAMBE MUNICIPALITY'. Electricity lines: ELEC USAGE BUS - PA (kWh, energy -> standard), ELECTR. USAGE BUS. - P.A. CAPACITY CHARGE (kVA -> demand; the PDF text often glues its date into the description and wraps 'CHARGE' to the line end, both handled) and BASIC CHARGE (-> other). Readings are printed without the x100 meter factor (consumption = (new-old) x 100), so start/end readings are as printed and total kWh comes from the ledger units; a catch-up bill with two reading rows keeps the latest row's readings while total kWh covers both. Only one reading date is printed (read_end). IDENTITY x_elec_resid_r = TOTAL DUE - Opening Balance - every non-electricity ledger line (payments, other services, interest, rebates) - the VAT line, i.e. the electricity total implied by the bill's own balance movement, independent of the electricity lines; 0.00 gap on all 9 electricity bills. 10 bills checked; 1 bill of a second account carries only rates/water/refuse (no electricity row, by design).",
